+// Gtavport: every translated pixel shader that writes colour keeps a discard (the alpha-to-mask clip
+// behind a uniform), so the GPU runs it before the depth/stencil test ("late Z"). GTA's deferred lights
+// mark their volume in the stencil and then shade only the marked pixels; with late tests each light
+// shaded its whole volume. In a room with a lit Christmas tree (dozens of small lights) the HDR
+// lighting pass went from ~3 ms to ~80 ms per frame on the Odin 2. Pipelines that write neither depth
+// nor stencil get the shader with EarlyFragmentTests: the same image (nothing they could discard
+// changes the depth or stencil buffer), tested before shading.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gtav_native_early_tests, true, "GTAV",
+                    "Native renderer: depth/stencil test before the pixel shader in pipelines that write neither "
+                    "depth nor stencil (the translated shaders' discard otherwise forces the test after it)");
